{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"deploy-helpers","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Deploy Helpers","description":"Publish a folder to Hostinger or any SSH server, Netlify, Vercel, GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages, Firebase or Surge. Always asks first.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:deployHelpers.menu","onCommand:deployHelpers.build","onCommand:deployHelpers.showSettings","onCommand:deployHelpers.rsync","onCommand:deployHelpers.rsyncDelete","onCommand:deployHelpers.scp","onCommand:deployHelpers.hostinger","onCommand:deployHelpers.sshOpen","onCommand:deployHelpers.netlifyPreview","onCommand:deployHelpers.netlifyProd","onCommand:deployHelpers.vercelPreview","onCommand:deployHelpers.vercelProd","onCommand:deployHelpers.ghPages","onCommand:deployHelpers.cloudflare","onCommand:deployHelpers.firebase","onCommand:deployHelpers.surge"],"permissions":["terminal"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"deployHelpers.menu","title":"Deploy...","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.build","title":"Build Before Deploying...","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.showSettings","title":"Show the Deploy Settings","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.rsync","title":"Deploy: Server over SSH: rsync (fast, only sends changes)","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.rsyncDelete","title":"Deploy: Server over SSH: rsync and delete files that are gone","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.scp","title":"Deploy: Server over SSH: scp (works where rsync is missing)","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.hostinger","title":"Deploy: Hostinger shared hosting (scp over SSH)","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.sshOpen","title":"Deploy: Open a shell on the server","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.netlifyPreview","title":"Deploy: Netlify: preview deploy","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.netlifyProd","title":"Deploy: Netlify: deploy to production","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.vercelPreview","title":"Deploy: Vercel: preview deploy","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.vercelProd","title":"Deploy: Vercel: deploy to production","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.ghPages","title":"Deploy: GitHub Pages: publish the folder","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.cloudflare","title":"Deploy: Cloudflare Pages: deploy the folder","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.firebase","title":"Deploy: Firebase Hosting: deploy","category":"Deploy Helpers"},{"command":"deployHelpers.surge","title":"Deploy: Surge: publish the folder","category":"Deploy Helpers"}],"configuration":{"title":"Deploy Helpers","properties":{"deployHelpers.localDir":{"type":"string","default":"dist","description":"The folder to publish, relative to your project, for example dist or build."},"deployHelpers.sshHost":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"For SSH targets: user@host, for example u123456789@123.45.67.89."},"deployHelpers.sshPort":{"type":"number","default":22,"description":"The SSH port. Hostinger shared hosting uses 65002."},"deployHelpers.remotePath":{"type":"string","default":"","description":"The folder on the server, for example domains/example.com/public_html."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Deploy Helpers: publish a folder to Hostinger (or any server over SSH), Netlify, Vercel, GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages, Firebase or Surge.\n// Every deploy shows you the exact command and asks before it runs, then types it in the terminal. Passwords are never stored or typed:\n// use SSH keys or log in to each service once with its own tool.\n\nconst HOST = /^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+@[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$/;\nconst REMOTE = /^\\/?[A-Za-z0-9._/~-]+$/;\nconst LOCAL = /^[A-Za-z0-9._/-]+$/;\n\n/** Reads and checks the settings. Returns { ok, error?, host, port, remote, dir }. */\nfunction settings(get) {\n  const host = String(get('deployHelpers.sshHost') || '').trim();\n  const port = Number(get('deployHelpers.sshPort')) || 22;\n  const remote = String(get('deployHelpers.remotePath') || '').trim();\n  const dir = String(get('deployHelpers.localDir') || 'dist').trim().replace(/\\\\/g, '/').replace(/\\/+$/, '') || 'dist';\n  const errors = [];\n  if (!LOCAL.test(dir) || dir.includes('..')) errors.push('deployHelpers.localDir must be a plain folder name such as dist or build.');\n  return { host, port, remote, dir, errors };\n}\n\nfunction sshProblems(s) {\n  const errors = [...s.errors];\n  if (!HOST.test(s.host)) errors.push('Set deployHelpers.sshHost to user@host, for example u123456789@123.45.67.89.');\n  if (!(Number.isInteger(s.port) && s.port >= 1 && s.port <= 65535)) errors.push('deployHelpers.sshPort must be a port number.');\n  if (!REMOTE.test(s.remote) || s.remote.includes('..')) errors.push('Set deployHelpers.remotePath to the folder on the server, for example domains/example.com/public_html.');\n  return errors;\n}\n\n/** Commands. Each takes the checked settings and returns { title, cmd, warn? }. */\nconst TARGETS = {\n  rsync: { label: 'Server over SSH: rsync (fast, only sends changes)', ssh: true, build: (s) => `rsync -avz -e \"ssh -p ${s.port}\" ${s.dir}/ ${s.host}:${s.remote}/` },\n  rsyncDelete: { label: 'Server over SSH: rsync and delete files that are gone', ssh: true, warn: 'This DELETES files on the server that are not in your local folder.', build: (s) => `rsync -avz --delete -e \"ssh -p ${s.port}\" ${s.dir}/ ${s.host}:${s.remote}/` },\n  scp: { label: 'Server over SSH: scp (works where rsync is missing)', ssh: true, build: (s) => `scp -P ${s.port} -r ${s.dir}/. ${s.host}:${s.remote}/` },\n  hostinger: { label: 'Hostinger shared hosting (scp over SSH)', ssh: true, build: (s) => `scp -P ${s.port} -r ${s.dir}/. ${s.host}:${s.remote}/` },\n  sshOpen: { label: 'Open a shell on the server', ssh: true, noDir: true, build: (s) => `ssh -p ${s.port} ${s.host}` },\n  netlifyPreview: { label: 'Netlify: preview deploy', build: (s) => `npx netlify deploy --dir=${s.dir}` },\n  netlifyProd: { label: 'Netlify: deploy to production', warn: 'This publishes to your live Netlify site.', build: (s) => `npx netlify deploy --dir=${s.dir} --prod` },\n  vercelPreview: { label: 'Vercel: preview deploy', build: () => 'npx vercel' },\n  vercelProd: { label: 'Vercel: deploy to production', warn: 'This publishes to your live Vercel site.', build: () => 'npx vercel --prod' },\n  ghPages: { label: 'GitHub Pages: publish the folder', warn: 'This pushes the folder to the gh-pages branch.', build: (s) => `npx gh-pages -d ${s.dir}` },\n  cloudflare: { label: 'Cloudflare Pages: deploy the folder', build: (s) => `npx wrangler pages deploy ${s.dir}` },\n  firebase: { label: 'Firebase Hosting: deploy', warn: 'This publishes to your live Firebase site.', build: () => 'npx firebase-tools deploy --only hosting' },\n  surge: { label: 'Surge: publish the folder', build: (s) => `npx surge ${s.dir}` },\n};\n\nexports._test = { settings, sshProblems, TARGETS, HOST, REMOTE };\n\nexports.activate = function (context) {\n  const read = () => settings((k) => ferrum.settings.get(k));\n\n  async function deploy(id) {\n    const t = TARGETS[id];\n    const s = read();\n    const errors = [...s.errors, ...(t.ssh ? sshProblems(s).filter((e) => !s.errors.includes(e)) : [])].filter((e) => !(t.noDir && e.includes('localDir')));\n    if (errors.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage(errors[0], 'warn');\n    const cmd = t.build(s);\n    const ok = await ferrum.window.confirm((t.warn ? t.warn + '\\n\\n' : '') + 'This will run in the terminal, from the folder you opened:\\n\\n' + cmd, 'Run it');\n    if (!ok) return;\n    await ferrum.terminal.run(cmd);\n  }\n\n  for (const id of Object.keys(TARGETS)) context.subscriptions.push(ferrum.commands.register('deployHelpers.' + id, () => deploy(id)));\n  context.subscriptions.push(\n    ferrum.commands.register('deployHelpers.menu', async () => {\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(Object.entries(TARGETS).map(([id, t]) => ({ label: t.label, detail: t.warn || '', id })), { placeholder: 'Deploy ' + read().dir + '/ to...' });\n      if (pick) await deploy(pick.id);\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('deployHelpers.build', async () => {\n      const pick = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick([{ label: 'npm run build', cmd: 'npm run build' }, { label: 'npm ci && npm run build', cmd: 'npm ci && npm run build' }, { label: 'composer install --no-dev -o', cmd: 'composer install --no-dev -o' }, { label: 'cargo build --release', cmd: 'cargo build --release' }], { placeholder: 'Build before deploying' });\n      if (pick) await ferrum.terminal.run(pick.cmd);\n    }),\n    ferrum.commands.register('deployHelpers.showSettings', async () => {\n      const s = read();\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Deploying ' + s.dir + '/ to ' + (s.host || '(sshHost not set)') + ':' + (s.remote || '(remotePath not set)') + ' on port ' + s.port + '.');\n    }),\n  );\n};\n\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Deploy Helpers\n\nPut the folder you built online with one command from the palette. Before anything runs, you see **the exact command** and confirm it; then it is typed in the terminal where you watch it work.\n\n## Targets\n\n- **Servers over SSH**: rsync (fast, sends only changes), rsync that also deletes remote files that are gone (warned), scp for machines without rsync, and a **Hostinger shared hosting** variant. Set `deployHelpers.sshHost`, `sshPort` (Hostinger uses 65002) and `remotePath` (for Hostinger something like `domains/yoursite.com/public_html`).\n- **Netlify** (preview or production), **Vercel** (preview or production), **GitHub Pages** (`gh-pages`), **Cloudflare Pages** (`wrangler`), **Firebase Hosting**, **Surge**. These tools are run with `npx`, and you log in once with each tool's own command.\n- **Build Before Deploying...** types a common build command.\n\n## Passwords\n\nThis extension **never stores or types a password**. Use SSH keys for servers (`ssh-keygen`, then add the public key in your host's panel). If the server asks for a password it asks in the terminal, which only you type in.\n\n## Safety\n\nSettings are checked: a host must look like `user@host`, the remote path and local folder can only use plain path characters, so a setting cannot smuggle in a second command.\n\n## Permissions\n\n**terminal**. It does not read any file.\n"}}}